facts:
A **translation** adds or subtracts the stated distance: add the horizontal distance to $x$ for right and subtract it for left; add the vertical distance to $y$ for up and subtract it for down.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.6]
\draw[gray!30,very thin](-5,-5)grid(5,5);
\draw[<->](-5.5,0)--(5.5,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->](0,-5.5)--(0,5.5)node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed,->](-3,-2)--(1.9,-2);
\draw[dashed,->](2,-2)--(2,1.9);
\fill(-3,-2)circle(3pt)node[below left]{$P$};
\fill(2,2)circle(3pt)node[above right]{$P'$};
\node[below] at (-0.5,-2.15) {right};
\node[right] at (2.2,1) {up};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Reflecting in the **$x$-axis** keeps $x$ the same and changes the **sign of $y$**: $(x, y) \to (x, -y)$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.62]
\draw[gray!30,very thin](-4,-4)grid(4,4);
\draw[<->](-4.6,0)--(4.6,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->](0,-4.6)--(0,4.6)node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed](-2.5,2)--(-2.5,-2);
\fill(-2.5,2)circle(3pt)node[above left]{$P$};
\fill(-2.5,-2)circle(3pt)node[below left]{$P'$};
\node[below right,font=\small] at (0.3,-0.1) {mirror line};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Reflecting in the **$y$-axis** keeps $y$ the same and changes the **sign of $x$**: $(x, y) \to (-x, y)$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.62]
\draw[gray!30,very thin](-4,-4)grid(4,4);
\draw[<->](-4.6,0)--(4.6,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->](0,-4.6)--(0,4.6)node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed](-2.5,2.5)--(2.5,2.5);
\fill(-2.5,2.5)circle(3pt)node[above left]{$P$};
\fill(2.5,2.5)circle(3pt)node[above right]{$P'$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (0.25,-2.2) {mirror line};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Triangle $ABC$ has vertices $A(-4,-1)$, $B(-2,-1)$ and $C(-4,1)$. Translate it $5$ units right and $2$ units up. Write the image coordinates and draw the image.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[draw={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204},very thin,xstep=6mm,ystep=6mm](-5,-4)grid(5,4);
\draw[black,<->](-5.4,0)--(5.4,0);\path(5.4,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[black,<->](0,-4.4)--(0,4.4);\path(0,4.4)node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-2,2,4}{\draw[black](\v,.08)--(\v,-.08);\path(\v,-.08)node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont]{$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}{\draw[black](.08,\v)--(-.08,\v);\path(-.08,\v)node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont]{$\v$};}
\draw[black,thick](-4,-1)--(-2,-1)--(-4,1)--cycle;
\path(-4,-1)node[below left]{$A$}(-2,-1)node[below right]{$B$}(-4,1)node[above left]{$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Slide every vertex $5$ units right and $2$ units up.
$\begin{aligned}A'&=(-4+5,-1+2)=(1,1)\\B'&=(-2+5,-1+2)=(3,1)\\C'&=(-4+5,1+2)=(1,3)\end{aligned}$
Plot the image vertices and join them in the same order.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{imageblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[draw={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204},very thin,xstep=6mm,ystep=6mm](-5,-4)grid(5,4);
\draw[black,<->](-5.4,0)--(5.4,0);\path(5.4,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[black,<->](0,-4.4)--(0,4.4);\path(0,4.4)node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-2,2,4}{\draw[black](\v,.08)--(\v,-.08);\path(\v,-.08)node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont]{$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}{\draw[black](.08,\v)--(-.08,\v);\path(-.08,\v)node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont]{$\v$};}
\draw[black,thick](-4,-1)--(-2,-1)--(-4,1)--cycle;
\path(-4,-1)node[below left]{$A$}(-2,-1)node[below right]{$B$}(-4,1)node[above left]{$C$};
\draw[imageblue,thick](1,1)--(3,1)--(1,3)--cycle;
\path(1,1)node[below right]{$A'$}(3,1)node[right]{$B'$}(1,3)node[above right]{$C'$};
\draw[imageblue,dashed,->](-4,-1)--(1,-1)--(1,1);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

